<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>French AI company announces new, private model</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:279e5f81aa872af8edd972b3a7fe3f1fbfe097e6a07b9e8124a7cb8f82b86073</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/french-ai-company-announces-new-private-model/a-79569597--64cfbccdac1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/french-ai-company-announces-new-private-model/a-79569597?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The company's new model, named "Le Chonk," is its first release in five months. Mistral says it outruns some of its Chinese competitors in several areas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Southeast Asia's haze crisis: Have lessons been learned?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bb3b1a7678acbcfe50f0456b63ef1420a2d33cf0628910de12e4d5852cb5b7c</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/southeast-asia-s-haze-crisis-have-lessons-been-learned/a-79564992--f0834d091bdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/southeast-asia-s-haze-crisis-have-lessons-been-learned/a-79564992?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Eleven years after catastrophic fires prompted promises of tougher action, Southeast Asia is again choking on transboundary haze, raising questions about whether the region has learned the lessons of 2015.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>As more Iranian women reject hijab rules, regime looks at new ways to force compliance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e635f2f364b181b3fe6cc4adcaa1d9b1ab26255db231faaf84759c0b8fb2f6f</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-more-iranian-women-reject-hijab-rules-regime-looks-at-new-ways-to-force-compliance/a-79564962--9c09f80416a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-more-iranian-women-reject-hijab-rules-regime-looks-at-new-ways-to-force-compliance/a-79564962?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As more women in Iran reject rules on wearing hijab headscarves, hardliners are shifting focus from "morality police" street enforcement towards social pressure in workplaces, services and businesses.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Opposition leaders march toward Election Commission</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39bdfb75dcf8e1dc2c5a11d9641ba7ed9598e025e97dae851fdcb5810d3f718d</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T05:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-leaders-march-toward-election-commission/live-79557629--9bfc41d38401.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-leaders-march-toward-election-commission/live-79557629?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's opposition is amping up pressure on Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar to resign over alleged voter roll manipulation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>ICC unseals Taliban leaders' warrants over persecuting women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf430b6e8b5a8ab6f793696d911b18e6d301e1f1b438c2c1779e67b88f5130a9</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T21:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/icc-unseals-taliban-leaders-warrants-over-persecuting-women/a-79556631--069482e3bddf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/icc-unseals-taliban-leaders-warrants-over-persecuting-women/a-79556631?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The court gave more details on the warrants for four Taliban leaders accused of the crime against humanity of gender persecution of women, girls and the LGBTQ+ community. The Islamist group rejected the warrants.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3ab6a39c4d3032243ae18cc557a87aacffc7dbb489df810fc260aaf0325f90e</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What China's new military foothold in Laos means for Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cb420b3c2b3da2be2ab69ded183a38073e829a7f78ee02c036f77ee40623b05</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-china-s-new-military-foothold-in-laos-means-for-southeast-asia/a-79548259--642cd34d5dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-china-s-new-military-foothold-in-laos-means-for-southeast-asia/a-79548259?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing says its new Laos facility will train pilots. Analysts see a broader signal: China's growing military presence in mainland Southeast Asia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Top court hears petitions against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c459da8503d0171c620971683d9806b1990a047d4cf0c85291c3a505212ba84</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T05:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-top-court-hears-petitions-against-chief-election-commissioner-gyanesh-kumar/live-79542552--db693202576d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-top-court-hears-petitions-against-chief-election-commissioner-gyanesh-kumar/live-79542552?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Supreme Court heard pleas against India's beleagured poll body chief over alleged unilateral decisions related to the large-scale revision of voter lists.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: FBI arrests woman accused of spying for China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7117913888873e7a556d060f6c00981b0b6df61502c8af8444baefaf44752a9a</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T03:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-fbi-arrests-woman-accused-of-spying-for-china/a-79541849--28beb0c09d9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-fbi-arrests-woman-accused-of-spying-for-china/a-79541849?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A California woman was arrested at Los Angeles International Airport, just before departing for China, with the US officials accusing her of spying on Taiwan's president's son.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>A brutal assault reignites fears over women's safety in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe7f6cb5bce7aa02fc3277cd12dcece65f8de19777b343b0a9a88a31a7bc8a45</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471--bceecddefb45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A string of sexual violence cases has revived questions about women's safety in India, fueling fear, protests and demands for action.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Lawyer of Junaid Hafeez, a Pakistai scholar imprisoned for 13 years, is hopeful for his release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec738f833b1fd8d2a5c5a937420b44296756c09e9a3650d95343aee5a0bdb032</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207--6c93b577eab6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fulbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea has recently completed two road bridges easing transport to strategic allies Russia and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32b6364eb60b241f4a1c766784daed2445f33576d15b276e8ac8ec1b69d3ac36</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-/a-79473981--09998bc65869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-china/a-79473981?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two recently opened bridges are expected to ease trade and transport between North Korea and its powerful neighbors. The new connections come as Pyongyang builds strategic ties with China and Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Women and children displaced by Nepal's floods say safe housing, privacy and stability remain out of reach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae3f0b02e37b702af046f0b2b434d0214372570718592d22912b045d54c91255</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-/a-79474014--5ad51afec87b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-reach/a-79474014?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Families living in temporary shelters in northern Nepal say safety and privacy remain out of reach as concerns about trafficking and abuse mount.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Global trade weathers Iran, Ukraine and Trump's tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd13b8a07c7a543d98dd011a38adddf7879bfd2855a29fe75b1317bfab279448</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643--538fe77d9a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past six years, COVID, two wars and Donald Trump's tariffs have shaken world trade. With globalization already stalling, is this a temporary shock or the start of a great reversal?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48601a0841cb6a0ed9185cbeccf6bcf0351c2e8e14ea6f0e8014f4319fa9e430</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
